  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Does every finite group G contain a pair of conjugate elements a, b such that\nπ(G) = π(⟨a, b⟩)? This is true for soluble groups.\n   Comment of 2013: it was proved in (A. Lucchini, M. Morigi, P. Shumyatsky, Forum\nMath., 24 (2012), 875–887) that every finite group G contains a 2-generator subgroup\nH such that π(G) = π(H).                                              P. Shumyatsky",
